      "Five of the 15 tests labelled flaky fail in every run on this machine: test_case_19, 20 and 21 (root cause time_tz: the clock is frozen at fixed instants inside the test, so the real time of day does not matter and they never pass) and test_case_14 and 15 (root cause timing: the test waits 0.02 s for work that takes 0.04 s). A method that only sees runs cannot tell them from real failures. They are counted as flaky because that is their label, and reported separately as flaky_label_but_fails_every_run.",
